provenance.prompt:
Create one original true-transparent RGBA production spritesheet for Moxie Capwell's right-facing basketball fall action. Strictly match supplied Moxie portrait and gameplay references: adult human woman, pale skin, lavender-purple eyes, very long thick lavender high ponytail with small gold tie, mature athletic build, purple-and-silver uniform with white side panels, purple wristbands, purple high-tops. Keep exact identity and consistent anatomy.

1990s arcade basketball pixel-cel sprites. Exact 1536x1024 canvas, 5 columns x 2 rows, ten distinct complete full-body poses in row-major order. Leave generous empty space around every pose: at least 45 transparent pixels from each figure to its cell boundaries, including leftmost hand, ponytail, and shoes. Keep each pose centered within its own cell, never touching any grid or canvas edge. Entire pose fits inside the cell. No overlap between poses. The bottom row also has roomy clear gutters.
No ball is drawn; separate game basketball only. No opponent, court, floor, shadow, background, glow, effects, text or labels. True transparent RGBA, alpha zero outside every figure.
A controlled nonviolent basketball stumble-and-fall, no injury:
0 off-balance recovery step after loose-ball collision, arms out;
1 stumble forward, one foot catches, hands spread;
2 lower center, bend knees, reach one hand toward floor;
3 knee touches down and opposite hand braces;
4 controlled side fall, hip lowers, ponytail arcs behind;
5 settle onto side with palm supporting, legs bent;
6 seated on hip, one hand plants, other hand visible and empty;
7 turn to one knee;
8 rise to low crouch;
9 balanced standing guard, calm face.
All ten figures are fully visible with complete hands, hair, and shoes.

